  "ingredients": [
    "2 cup almond flour",
    "1/2 teaspoon baking powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1/3 cup stevia/erythritol blend (such as Swerve)",
    "6 tablespoon butter",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 tablespoon lemon zest",
    "4 teaspoon lemon juice",
    "2 teaspoon dried rosemary (or fresh)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a large mixing bowl, measure out the almond flour, baking powder, and baking soda. Mix together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the granulated sweetener.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt the butter in the microwave (about 20 seconds). Add in the vanilla extract and mix together.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer the almond flour mixture to a small mixing bowl. Add the butter, lemon zest, lemon juice, and chopped rosemary to the emptied large mixing bowl. Slowly add the almond flour mixture back in, stirring constantly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-12.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keep mixing the dough together until all of the almond flour has been added.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-13.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shape the dough into a log, then wrap the dough tightly in plastic wrap. Place the wrapped dough in the freezer for 30 minutes, or until hard.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-14.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. Unwrap the dough. Cut the dough into slices using a sharp knife (a dull knife will cause the dough to crumble). If the dough is still crumbling, it may need to sit in the freezer for a little while longer.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-15.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grease a cookie sheet with salted butter (this adds a great hint of flavor to the bottom of the cookies). Alternatively, use a Silpat liner. Place the cut cookies onto the baking sheet. Bake for 15 minutes or until golden brown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread-18.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Allow the cookies to cool for about 10 minutes. Remove from the cookie sheet and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-rosemary-low-carb-shortbread/#wprm-recipe-50585-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
